text:
marco: Quick flag from the mobile QA sweep — when the left sidebar slides in on narrow widths the table's sticky header shifts down by ~6px after the animation. Happens on Android Chrome and iOS. screenshot: https://img.redwood.test/console/2026-06/header-shift-anim.gif

sylvie: I can repro on Pixel. Animation end seems to trigger a reflow; suspect toggling `overflow` on body/backdrop creates a new stacking context and sticky recomputes.

eli: Could we avoid the overlap by changing the pattern at small widths? My proposal: at <=440px use a bottom sheet for filters/columns, keep project nav in compact header chip; between 441-720px use a full-screen modal for nav so sticky header isn't active simultaneously.

zoe: 👍 to bottom sheet for filters. UX note: bottom sheet should include a clear two-line header: "Columns & density\nChoose visible columns and row density (saved per device)" — makes persistent behavior explicit. Also add a small help icon linking to docs.

marco: Dev note: if we do full-screen modal for mid widths, ensure we set `position: fixed; inset: 0` and change header `position` to `relative` while modal open so sticky doesn't fight. Also add `aria-hidden` on main content.

sylvie: CSS sketch:```css
@media (max-width: 440px) {
  .sheet-filters { position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 60vh; border-top-left-radius: 12px; }
}
@media (min-width: 441px) and (max-width: 720px) {
  .sidebar-modal { position: fixed; inset: 0; }
  .main-header { position: relative; }
}
```

eli: Accessibility checklist: focus trap in sheet/modal, ESC to close, set `aria-modal` for bottom sheet, announce title to screen readers. For the search icon we hide inline search <=480px and expose a magnifier button with `aria-label="Open search"`.

zoe: Hit target issue: compact rows are ~30px height. We should make the whole stacked row a single tap target >=44px and leave kebab as a separate small control. That should cut accidental kebab opens.

marco: Table overflow: long model IDs and URLs cause horizontal scroll in stacked layout. Suggest rendering tokens as truncated pills with `title` attr and a small copy icon. CSS: `.token { max-width: 160px; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }` and `word-break: break-word` for fallback. On tap show full value in a toast with copy.

sylvie: Also change clipboard microcopy from generic "Copied" to "Copied model ID" so users know which value was copied when multiple popups occur. Small but helpful.

eli: Experiment idea: two-week A/B: Variant A = stacked card layout (full-row tap target). Variant B = compact table with increased vertical padding to meet 44px. Metrics: navigation success, accidental kebab opens, time-to-action. I'll create a feature flag and metric events.

zoe: Gesture conflict: edge-swipe nav sometimes conflicts with row swipe actions. Implementation: only treat edge-swipe as nav when `touchstart.clientX < 20`. Otherwise route to row swipe. Also add a subtle left-edge affordance to hint nav.

marco: Keyboard/safe-area: for iOS Safari ensure `position: sticky` header respects `env(safe-area-inset-top)` and recompute offsets on visualViewport `resize` so keyboard doesn't hide inputs. Example JS: `visualViewport.addEventListener('resize', () => { document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--vv-offset', visualViewport.offsetTop + 'px'); });`

sylvie: Dev tasks summary: 1) implement breakpoint tokens + CSS for bottom sheet & full-screen modal, 2) header offset handling with visualViewport, 3) token truncation + copy pill and updated toast copy, 4) increase hit targets and A/B flag.

eli: I'll own A/B setup and metrics. Zoe, can you draft the accessibility checklist and quick usability script for 6 participants?

zoe: On it. Will include keyboard, screen reader, and one-handed reachability checks. Also will verify focus order when sheet/modal opens.

access-bot: Reminder: update design tokens doc (sources/design/tokens.md) and add an entry in sources/slack/product with screenshots and experiment plan.

marco: Great. I'll open a RFC PR this afternoon with the breakpoint token changes and a short demo GIF. Thanks all :thumbsup:
